sketch-orca oracle patch 0004: the FMA3 knob, SKETCH_ORCA_ORACLE_FMA3.
Modified for Sketch, 2026-11-06.

With SKETCH_ORCA_ORACLE_FMA3=0, the oracle calls _set_FMA3_enable(0) before anything else: in a
static initializer placed in the compiler's initialization segment (#pragma init_seg(compiler),
cli/oracle_fma3.cpp), which the CRT runs after its own initialization and before every other
static initializer of the program. The Universal CRT's x64 maths functions (exp, log, pow, sin,
cos and the rest) then take their SSE2 paths, not their FMA3 ones, whatever the CPU. "1" leaves
the CRT's own choice, as unset does. Any other value stops the oracle before it does anything
else, with exit code 78.

---
